WEBVTT

00:05.770 --> 00:07.940
You want to take over Mikazuki Temple?

00:08.430 --> 00:09.980
Are you serious about that, Yuzuki?

00:10.540 --> 00:11.240
Yeah.

00:11.240 --> 00:13.760
Taking over a temple is a lot of work.

00:13.760 --> 00:15.490
Why do you want to do it?

00:15.820 --> 00:17.430
Because I...

01:50.550 --> 01:54.000
<i>I haven't spoken with Akagami-kun 
at all since then.</i>

01:54.340 --> 01:55.510
Forget it!

01:56.060 --> 01:58.260
It's none of your business!

01:58.760 --> 02:02.850
<b>Episode 12:
No One Should Live Alone</b>

01:58.940 --> 02:02.260
<i>Is he mad? He must be mad.</i>

02:03.790 --> 02:05.390
I should apologize.

02:06.410 --> 02:11.110
Yeah, that's what I'll do. 
I'm sure he'll understand.

02:11.110 --> 02:14.360
Thank you so much.

02:12.910 --> 02:14.360
That's Akagami-kun's voice.

02:14.360 --> 02:16.990
It's fine. Just don't lose it again.

02:16.990 --> 02:18.430
I'll be careful.

02:18.990 --> 02:21.340
If you have any questions 
about how to use it,

02:21.190 --> 02:21.990
Thank you.

02:21.340 --> 02:22.990
I'd be willing to teach you.

02:24.370 --> 02:28.120
<i>Wait, what? Why am I running away?</i>

02:36.360 --> 02:40.840
<i>No decent posts on job hunting 
sites at the start of the year.</i>

02:41.290 --> 02:45.140
Since it's none of my business, 
I'll do what I want!

02:45.500 --> 02:48.390
<i>That was childish of me.</i>

02:48.390 --> 02:51.900
<i>All right! I'll talk to her today
so we can reconcile!</i>

02:53.470 --> 02:55.400
Good morning, Akagami-kun!

02:56.860 --> 02:59.300
G-Good morning.

02:59.300 --> 03:01.410
Let's do our best today.

03:02.370 --> 03:03.410
Right...

03:05.620 --> 03:06.910
Yuzuki-san?!

03:07.690 --> 03:10.490
It must be good luck to get buried 
under a pile of Buddhist objects.

03:11.800 --> 03:13.520
Are you all right?

03:13.520 --> 03:15.920
I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

03:15.920 --> 03:19.420
Um... Yuzuki-san, I'd like to speak with you.

03:19.690 --> 03:20.800
Hold it.

03:21.220 --> 03:22.380
Kiki-san?

03:22.380 --> 03:25.750
Yuzuki, could you take those 
to the storage shed?

03:26.460 --> 03:27.180
Okay.

03:27.570 --> 03:30.610
Akagami, come with me. We need to talk.

03:33.510 --> 03:35.810
What did you want to discuss?

03:37.050 --> 03:39.320
Did something happen between you and Yuzuki?

03:40.250 --> 03:42.630
Well, actually...

03:46.100 --> 03:52.080
<b>SIGH</b>

03:47.550 --> 03:49.940
Oh, so it's just a couple's quarrel.

03:49.940 --> 03:52.080
Actually, it's a regular quarrel.

03:52.080 --> 03:54.850
You two are totally in love, aren't you?

03:54.850 --> 03:59.690
At first, we were both just being stubborn, 
but it escalated this time.

03:59.690 --> 04:00.970
I see.

04:02.110 --> 04:05.470
Akagami, what's this?

04:05.770 --> 04:06.420
Boobs.

04:06.420 --> 04:09.400
That's right. It's me, Kiki.

04:09.400 --> 04:12.730
Yes, of course that's what I was thinking.

04:13.160 --> 04:15.940
Nun, head priest, master...

04:15.940 --> 04:19.260
I'm a single human perceived 
differently by different people,

04:19.260 --> 04:22.740
though apparently you could 
only recognize me as boobs.

04:22.490 --> 04:23.240
<i><b>Eep!</b></i>

04:22.740 --> 04:23.240
Eep!

04:23.530 --> 04:25.860
Point at the moon, and you see a finger.

04:25.860 --> 04:31.750
People get distracted by the pointing finger 
when a person points at the moon.

04:32.080 --> 04:36.700
I pointed at my breasts earlier because 
I knew you'd make that mistake.

04:36.700 --> 04:38.000
That's not fair!

04:38.530 --> 04:41.480
I'm telling you not to lose
sight of what matters.

04:41.480 --> 04:45.330
A finger is an obvious sign, 
but if you get too distracted,

04:45.330 --> 04:48.850
you'll never reach the moon 
you should be looking at.

04:48.850 --> 04:51.020
What does that mean?

04:51.020 --> 04:55.230
How do you see Yuzuki?

04:56.140 --> 04:59.340
Yuzuki-san is dependable.

04:59.340 --> 05:01.540
She can be a bit careless,

05:01.540 --> 05:05.240
but she has her head on straight 
and is always so positive.

05:07.570 --> 05:10.530
She's much stronger than I am.

05:10.990 --> 05:14.250
That's your bias speaking, Akagami.

05:14.250 --> 05:15.130
What?

05:15.590 --> 05:17.750
Kiki-san, you have a guest.

05:18.130 --> 05:19.770
What do they want?

05:20.030 --> 05:21.750
They want to leave the temple (ridan).

05:20.250 --> 05:21.750
<b>Ridan</b>

05:22.760 --> 05:24.200
This is our chance!

05:24.200 --> 05:25.130
What do you mean?!

05:25.520 --> 05:27.130
We can collect their ridan fee!

05:27.130 --> 05:30.960
They'll pay us to remove their family's 
grave and express their gratitude.

05:27.130 --> 05:33.890
Ridan

05:27.130 --> 05:33.890
"Ridan" is the act
of ending a relationship
between a temple
and its supporters.

05:27.130 --> 05:33.890
When the relationship
is ended, the supporters'
graves are removed
or transferred.

05:30.960 --> 05:33.890
Shouldn't we be unhappy about 
supporters leaving the temple?

05:33.890 --> 05:36.360
What matters right now is the money.

05:36.360 --> 05:38.320
This is a blessing from the Buddha.

05:38.320 --> 05:40.610
<i>Her perception is totally warped!</i>

05:40.610 --> 05:42.720
Leave it to me.

05:42.720 --> 05:45.720
I'll make them cough up a hundred 
times the market price.

05:45.720 --> 05:47.860
Master, I think that's a bit much!

05:55.140 --> 05:58.830
They're going to transfer their grave 
to another temple in their neighborhood.

05:59.300 --> 06:01.340
Our location's not good for them.

06:01.340 --> 06:03.800
Did our guests leave? Did they pay a ridan fee?

06:04.120 --> 06:06.070
What? No.

06:06.810 --> 06:11.050
My mom decided we wouldn't collect 
withdrawal fees from supporters

06:11.050 --> 06:13.090
since they're a token of their gratitude.

06:13.090 --> 06:15.060
That's true, but...

06:15.410 --> 06:20.440
They still came despite the poor location 
while my mom was around.

06:20.800 --> 06:24.940
But they said they can't trust 
Mikazuki Temple now.

06:27.910 --> 06:31.780
I'm not as good at this as my mom.

06:32.290 --> 06:36.290
I thought I was doing my 
best to earn their trust,

06:37.470 --> 06:39.290
but I'm still not doing nearly enough.

06:39.730 --> 06:43.530
All right. I'll have to work even harder.

06:43.980 --> 06:45.250
Yuzuki-san...

06:48.240 --> 06:51.260
Yuzuki, stop training after today.

06:51.620 --> 06:54.010
I won't instruct you anymore.

06:55.260 --> 06:56.010
What?

06:56.460 --> 06:58.330
But why, Master?

06:58.330 --> 07:00.520
You'll have to figure that out yourself.

07:08.540 --> 07:11.060
Taking over a temple is a lot of work.

07:11.060 --> 07:12.490
Why do you want to do it?

07:12.490 --> 07:14.170
Because I...

07:14.900 --> 07:18.500
<i>How did I answer her then?</i>

07:24.760 --> 07:27.710
Oh, right. I don't have training today.

07:30.100 --> 07:33.010
<i>No, I don't have time to be depressed.</i>

07:33.010 --> 07:36.260
<i>I have a lot of things to do.</i>

07:36.780 --> 07:40.520
So I'll be doing my best again this year.

07:40.520 --> 07:42.210
What exactly will you do?

07:42.210 --> 07:44.220
Well, uh...

07:44.220 --> 07:47.760
You'll commit harakiri and write your 
New Year's calligraphy in blood, right?

07:47.760 --> 07:50.030
Japan is so exotic.

07:50.750 --> 07:52.400
I don't think I'll be doing that.

07:52.770 --> 07:55.940
She probably means airing out the floor 
cushions, maintaining the tatami mats,

07:53.950 --> 07:58.540
<b>Over 100 cushions total!</b>

07:55.410 --> 07:58.540
<b>Mikazuki Temple is
in the 80-tatami class!</b>

07:55.940 --> 07:58.540
and polishing the Buddhist objects.

07:58.800 --> 08:02.660
That's right. There's a lot to do 
at a temple besides train.

08:02.960 --> 08:06.170
But it should be easy thanks to Akagami.

08:06.170 --> 08:07.140
Huh?

08:07.140 --> 08:10.240
The whole temple's sparkling 
clean most of the time.

08:10.240 --> 08:14.100
He regularly airs out the cushions and mats.

08:14.100 --> 08:16.800
And I helped him polish the Buddhist objects.

08:17.190 --> 08:19.180
But there's a lot of other things to do.

08:19.180 --> 08:21.430
We'll be done in a snap if we do it together.

08:21.430 --> 08:26.090
Oh, right. Wait, where's Akagami-kun?

08:26.090 --> 08:29.320
He followed Kiki-san on her business.

08:29.600 --> 08:30.650
Why?

08:30.650 --> 08:33.820
Who knows? I'd like to know, too,

08:34.590 --> 08:37.030
but my messages aren't showing as read.

08:37.340 --> 08:39.250
I keep sending them, too.

08:39.660 --> 08:42.120
You have Akagami's contact information?

08:42.120 --> 08:42.790
Huh?

08:43.240 --> 08:47.400
Why do you have that? Why don't I have it?

08:47.400 --> 08:50.300
I don't have his, either. I want it, too.

08:50.420 --> 08:52.050
No fair!

08:52.050 --> 08:54.300
Oh, I have it.

08:54.300 --> 08:56.550
Exactly why do you have it?

08:58.060 --> 09:01.530
You shouldn't get the jump on us like that.

09:01.530 --> 09:04.600
Just because you've already 
conquered Akagami...

09:04.600 --> 09:06.810
Okay, I'd like to correct that!

09:06.810 --> 09:09.310
<b>CHATTER\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hCHATTER</b>

09:07.860 --> 09:09.310
Help me, Yuzu-nee!

09:10.390 --> 09:12.070
Yuzu-nee?

09:12.420 --> 09:14.330
I'd expect nothing less from Akagami-kun.

09:14.330 --> 09:16.320
He does a perfect job, and everybody loves him.

09:16.740 --> 09:18.820
But I can work just as hard.

09:24.570 --> 09:26.880
<i>It really is spotless.</i>

09:29.740 --> 09:31.840
<i>It's okay, Akagami-kun.</i>

09:32.490 --> 09:34.880
I'll figure something out.

09:35.240 --> 09:38.140
<i>That's right. I have to do something.</i>

09:38.460 --> 09:41.740
<i>After all, my mom managed to do this alone.</i>

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Supermarket clerk

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Call center

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Fast food

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Convenience store

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Mover

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Illustrator

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Maid café

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Newspaper delivery

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Road work

09:49.350 --> 09:51.110
Cram school lecturer

10:04.370 --> 10:06.870
<b>Specializing in High-paying Jobs</b>

10:20.340 --> 10:24.060
<b>All things are without a self.</b>

10:24.750 --> 10:28.310
Master, please allow Yuzuki-san 
to resume her training!

10:28.770 --> 10:30.090
Please!

10:30.090 --> 10:31.310
This isn't the place for this.

10:33.810 --> 10:36.040
And don't make me say it again.

10:36.040 --> 10:38.780
Yuzuki doesn't currently have the right.

10:39.140 --> 10:43.280
I'm not sure you have the right to be 
our temple's head priest, so please!

10:43.280 --> 10:45.290
Watch it. I'll end your training, too.

10:45.810 --> 10:49.290
Yuzuki has to figure this out for herself.

10:50.450 --> 10:52.290
There's no need for me to get involved.

10:52.650 --> 10:54.550
Can't you please make an exception?

10:54.550 --> 10:56.050
Pay the check, okay?

10:56.300 --> 10:58.020
Master!

10:58.020 --> 10:59.550
Oh, it's raining.

11:01.050 --> 11:01.620
Hello—

11:01.620 --> 11:03.300
<i>You finally answered!</i>

11:03.570 --> 11:04.770
<i>Tsukuyo-san?</i>

11:04.770 --> 11:06.660
<i>I'm sorry. I've been busy.</i>

11:06.660 --> 11:08.310
Something more important is happening!

11:08.310 --> 11:11.210
<i>Yuzu-nee has gone missing!</i>

11:19.910 --> 11:22.530
<i>She was acting weird this morning.</i>

11:22.820 --> 11:24.790
<i>Do you have any idea where she went?</i>

11:25.260 --> 11:26.890
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

11:30.270 --> 11:35.840
<i>Tell me, Akagami. How do you see Yuzuki?</i>

11:35.840 --> 11:38.580
<i>Yuzuki-san is dependable.</i>

11:38.580 --> 11:41.110
<i>She can be a bit careless,</i>

11:41.110 --> 11:44.300
<i>but she has her head on straight 
and is always so positive.</i>

12:02.650 --> 12:05.040
I'm so cold. What am I going to do?

12:05.040 --> 12:07.790
I think I have a fever.

12:09.630 --> 12:11.310
<i>I need to try harder.</i>

12:12.060 --> 12:16.490
<i>I need to be able to do everything 
myself so people will trust me.</i>

12:17.830 --> 12:20.970
<i>Otherwise, I'll never be like Mom.</i>

12:24.650 --> 12:27.460
<i>Damn it. I don't know where 
else she could've gone.</i>

12:29.700 --> 12:30.650
<i>Wait...</i>

12:34.850 --> 12:38.090
<i>She was strong and pretty. 
There wasn't anything she couldn't do.</i>

12:38.090 --> 12:40.350
<i>Everyone trusted her.</i>

12:40.950 --> 12:43.360
<i>Mom was perfect.</i>

12:44.210 --> 12:46.610
I'm shutting down Mikazuki Temple.

12:46.610 --> 12:48.870
Prepare to move, everyone.

12:49.370 --> 12:50.210
Got it?

12:51.390 --> 12:54.180
Why, Mom? This is too sudden.

12:54.180 --> 12:56.080
It's already been decided.

12:56.080 --> 12:57.580
Wait, Mom!

12:57.580 --> 12:59.630
I'll take over the temple!

12:59.890 --> 13:01.130
You'll take over this temple?

13:02.340 --> 13:03.380
I'll...

13:03.730 --> 13:05.570
You can't do it, Yuzuki.

13:12.410 --> 13:14.970
You can't save Mikazuki Temple.

13:19.850 --> 13:21.870
<i>I can't do it?</i>

13:23.200 --> 13:27.430
<i>Tell me, Mom. Is it because 
I'm not good enough?</i>

13:28.210 --> 13:30.350
<i>Am I lacking something?</i>

13:31.690 --> 13:37.420
<i>Then I'll have to work harder 
and become perfect.</i>

13:37.810 --> 13:40.960
Yuzuki, stop training after today.

13:40.960 --> 13:43.420
<i>Harder and harder.</i>

13:43.890 --> 13:45.800
You can't do it, Yuzuki-san!

13:45.800 --> 13:48.470
<i>I'll work harder.</i>

13:48.810 --> 13:50.570
You can't do it, Yuzuki.

13:51.230 --> 13:55.020
<i>I'll work harder, so don't 
close down our temple.</i>

13:55.820 --> 13:57.570
<i>Please come back, Mom.</i>

13:59.580 --> 14:01.030
I'm so cold.

14:05.790 --> 14:09.630
<i>There's no reason for her to be there.</i>

14:10.340 --> 14:17.030
<i>After all, Yuzuki-san is 
much stronger than I am.</i>

14:25.210 --> 14:28.630
<i>That's your bias speaking, Akagami.</i>

14:36.990 --> 14:39.150
Akagami-kun?

14:40.130 --> 14:43.770
<i>What about Yuzuki-san 
have I even been looking at?</i>

14:45.100 --> 14:47.210
<i>She faked smiles even when 
she was losing heart.</i>

14:48.190 --> 14:50.660
<i>She acted tough to hide her lack of confidence.</i>

14:51.730 --> 14:54.370
<i>But she's actually so very...</i>

15:14.180 --> 15:17.230
You're warm, Akagami-kun.

15:28.670 --> 15:31.420
Nope, I can't get up. Not with this fever.

15:32.160 --> 15:35.160
Zzz...

15:35.160 --> 15:36.460
Akagami-kun?!

15:36.460 --> 15:38.160
Yuzuki-san, you're awake!

15:38.830 --> 15:40.910
<i>Oh, right. I need to apologize.</i>

15:41.380 --> 15:43.170
<i>I must start by apologizing.</i>

15:43.170 --> 15:44.170
I'm so—

15:44.170 --> 15:45.700
Ow!

15:47.580 --> 15:49.260
I'm sorry.

15:49.260 --> 15:51.680
No, I'm sorry.

15:59.660 --> 16:03.490
I feel like we haven't talked in a while.

16:06.430 --> 16:07.300
Right?

16:07.690 --> 16:15.950
Water

16:07.690 --> 16:15.950
Stays Cold For
10 Hours

16:07.690 --> 16:15.950
Forehead Ice Pack

16:07.690 --> 16:15.950
White Peach

16:08.260 --> 16:10.540
You took care of me all night?

16:10.540 --> 16:13.020
I fell asleep at some point.

16:13.020 --> 16:14.180
I'm sorry.

16:14.180 --> 16:15.950
Why are you apologizing?

16:15.950 --> 16:17.260
Because...

16:19.190 --> 16:22.250
I'm surprised you knew I'd be under the bridge.

16:22.250 --> 16:27.750
I didn't think you'd do 
something as stupid as I did,

16:28.210 --> 16:32.240
but I heard from Kurage-san 
that you're a bumbling idiot.

16:32.240 --> 16:33.760
A bumbling idiot?!

16:33.760 --> 16:38.510
And I have some attachment to that place.

16:39.940 --> 16:42.770
The first key to achieving enlightenment is...

16:44.140 --> 16:46.400
"No one should live alone."

16:46.700 --> 16:49.970
My father used to say that all the time.

16:50.400 --> 16:54.250
He used it as an excuse 
to build a harem, though.

16:55.850 --> 17:02.950
I hated the phrase, 
so I swore I'd live my life alone.

17:03.210 --> 17:05.620
But you tore down that idea.

17:08.110 --> 17:12.960
My world turned upside-down 
under that bridge.

17:15.750 --> 17:18.970
So please, Yuzuki-san, involve me in your life.

17:18.970 --> 17:20.590
Akagami-kun...

17:21.260 --> 17:24.820
You said you wouldn't leave me alone,

17:24.820 --> 17:28.110
but you're trying to 
isolate yourself right now.

17:28.830 --> 17:32.470
Please let me be part of your relationships.

17:34.650 --> 17:38.540
But it has nothing to do with you.

17:39.620 --> 17:44.310
This only happened because I'm not good enough.

17:44.750 --> 17:47.570
You didn't do anything wrong.

17:47.990 --> 17:53.150
You should be doing what you want, 
but you're so busy every day.

17:54.100 --> 17:56.250
I don't want to cause any more trouble for you.

17:56.250 --> 17:58.380
I'm doing this because I want to.

17:58.910 --> 18:03.740
I love this temple just as much as you do.

18:07.740 --> 18:12.400
Because I love Mikazuki Temple.

18:13.890 --> 18:15.460
<i>I remember now.</i>

18:17.940 --> 18:20.810
<i>It's so simple.</i>

18:22.660 --> 18:25.790
Thank you, Akagami-kun.

18:28.100 --> 18:29.820
Truly, thank you.

18:32.420 --> 18:34.830
We overheard your conversation!

18:35.670 --> 18:44.810
Pharmacy by the Temple

18:35.670 --> 18:44.810
Cold Medicine

18:36.210 --> 18:37.920
How long have you been there?

18:37.920 --> 18:41.930
Since Akagami-san put this inside you.

18:41.930 --> 18:43.240
You did?

18:43.240 --> 18:44.810
I didn't put anything in anyone!

18:45.470 --> 18:46.690
Yuzu-nee.

18:47.300 --> 18:48.510
Tsukuyo.

18:48.940 --> 18:50.190
Idiot!

18:51.970 --> 18:54.200
We were so worried about you.

18:54.200 --> 18:57.050
We were so worried.

18:57.050 --> 18:58.770
Punish her with tickles.

18:58.770 --> 19:02.430
Or perhaps you'd prefer porn DVD punishment?

19:05.370 --> 19:07.790
Listen, Yuzu-nee.

19:08.210 --> 19:08.960
Huh?

19:09.460 --> 19:13.410
We love Mikazuki Temple, too.

19:13.410 --> 19:16.590
You can't exclude us from helping you.

19:17.610 --> 19:18.960
Guys...

19:18.960 --> 19:24.100
If anything, it feels like 
you're the one being excluded.

19:20.340 --> 19:28.850
Everyone Already Exchanged Contact Information

19:20.340 --> 19:28.850
Ta-da!

19:24.100 --> 19:27.640
You're the only one who doesn't have 
Akagami's contact information.

19:27.640 --> 19:28.850
What?!

19:31.860 --> 19:34.480
Let me join you!

19:37.640 --> 19:39.750
You seem surprisingly energetic.

19:40.220 --> 19:41.240
Kiki-san.

19:41.580 --> 19:43.090
Um, Master...

19:43.090 --> 19:46.580
Kiki-san, I finally figured it out.

19:47.470 --> 19:52.900
I know why you stopped training 
me and what I'd lost sight of.

19:54.810 --> 19:56.650
When I couldn't do what my mom did,

19:57.390 --> 20:01.340
I panicked and worried about 
what others thought of me.

20:02.050 --> 20:04.250
But I simply want to preserve the relationship

20:04.650 --> 20:07.430
between this temple and everyone 
as the head priest.

20:08.730 --> 20:14.230
Please train me again.

20:18.180 --> 20:19.110
Master!

20:19.700 --> 20:24.500
Fix your health first. 
Then we'll finish your training.

20:27.310 --> 20:28.990
Thank you!

20:31.070 --> 20:33.500
Settle down. Just rest.

20:33.880 --> 20:35.430
Good grief.

20:35.430 --> 20:38.120
Kiki-san, thank y—

20:38.120 --> 20:39.580
No need to thank me.

20:39.990 --> 20:41.010
But...

20:41.770 --> 20:44.010
The selfish desire for recognition

20:44.010 --> 20:48.510
is the farthest one can get 
from achieving enlightenment.

20:49.270 --> 20:54.930
Yuzuki simply realized how 
a head priest should truly be.

20:55.830 --> 20:59.940
I didn't do anything.

21:10.300 --> 21:12.620
Should you be up and about already?

21:12.890 --> 21:15.370
Yeah. My fever's gone down.

21:16.270 --> 21:19.010
I'm going to quit looking for a job.

21:19.010 --> 21:19.880
What?

21:20.580 --> 21:25.530
I'll ask our supporters for donations 
to repair the principle figure.

21:26.060 --> 21:29.140
I'm not sure they will.

21:29.620 --> 21:33.140
It'll be difficult. I agree.

21:33.140 --> 21:39.150
That's why I thought I had to sacrifice 
myself to protect Mikazuki Temple.

21:39.540 --> 21:40.650
Right.

21:41.190 --> 21:43.210
But that was wrong.

21:43.610 --> 21:48.770
There's no future when something's 
acquired through that kind of sacrifice.

21:50.380 --> 21:55.910
The fifth key to achieving enlightenment is 
"Don't run from your own weaknesses."

21:56.510 --> 21:59.920
We'll all protect Mikazuki Temple together.

21:59.920 --> 22:02.140
Yes, together.

22:04.060 --> 22:05.860
You forgot something.

22:07.500 --> 22:09.180
Oh, sorry.

22:09.450 --> 22:10.710
Hey, whoa!

22:15.740 --> 22:16.600
That was on purpose.

22:16.600 --> 22:18.460
Obviously not!

22:19.420 --> 22:20.730
Akagami-san.

22:21.690 --> 22:23.660
My goodbye kiss.

22:24.500 --> 22:27.020
Kurage, we're holding a family 
meeting when you get home.

22:29.820 --> 22:32.530
Kurage-san, don't you tease me, too.

22:32.530 --> 22:34.200
You're such a dummy, Akagami-san.

22:34.200 --> 22:36.660
Dummy, dummy, dummy.

22:36.660 --> 22:38.330
Mia, are you ready yet?

22:38.330 --> 22:40.090
I'll be right there.

22:45.730 --> 22:48.110
I-I'm sorry!

22:49.370 --> 22:50.500
Are you okay?

22:50.500 --> 22:52.270
Oh, this is nothing.

22:53.550 --> 22:55.760
Ow...

22:55.760 --> 22:57.310
It's suddenly nighttime?

23:03.350 --> 23:05.680
There, there. Wanna suck on these?

23:05.680 --> 23:06.660
No, thank you!

23:06.660 --> 23:10.320
Mia, we're visiting our dear 
supporters. Don't be late.

23:10.320 --> 23:11.740
Y-Yes, ma'am.

23:11.740 --> 23:14.250
Good luck on your first errand.

23:14.250 --> 23:16.080
Thanks for waiting, everyone.

23:16.450 --> 23:18.140
I'll be back later.

23:18.140 --> 23:19.900
Okay. Be careful.

23:19.900 --> 23:22.900
And, um... While I'm gone...

23:22.900 --> 23:24.090
I'll handle the chores.

23:24.090 --> 23:24.590
Huh?

23:25.100 --> 23:27.840
Don't worry about Mikazuki Temple.

23:28.590 --> 23:32.220
You're right. In that case, 
I'm counting on you.

23:32.570 --> 23:33.340
Sure.

23:34.060 --> 23:38.580
Yuzuki-oneechan is the only one who didn't 
have a sexual experience this morning.

23:38.580 --> 23:40.640
Kurage, what are you saying?!

23:40.640 --> 23:43.770
We don't know that yet. For example...

23:47.330 --> 23:48.900
See?

23:51.250 --> 23:52.660
Worldly thoughts, begone!

23:53.000 --> 23:57.850
Akagami-kun, you idiot!
